---
// Download cards (#517). Static: /download.js (public/) fills each platform from its manifest
// in /updates/ (windows.json, android.json, linux.json, written by the release scripts); a card
// stays hidden until its manifest is online. External script: the server's CSP forbids inline
// code.
---

<div class="sg-downloads not-content">
  <section class="sg-platform" id="windows" hidden>
    <h2>Windows</h2>
    <a class="sg-button" id="windows-link" href="#">Download for Windows</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="windows-meta"></p>
    <p>
      Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, AVX2-capable processor. The installer needs no administrator
      rights. If Windows shows "Windows protected your PC", click "More info" then "Run anyway":
      the installer has no Windows signing certificate. After that, the app updates itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-platform" id="android" hidden>
    <h2>Android</h2>
    <a class="sg-button" id="android-link" href="#">Download for Android</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="android-meta"></p>
    <p>
      Android 7 or newer, 64-bit (ARM) processor. On the first download, allow the browser to
      install apps; after that, the app offers its own updates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-platform" id="linux" hidden>
    <h2>Linux</h2>
    <a class="sg-button" id="linux-link" href="#">Download the AppImage</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="linux-meta"></p>
    <p>
      64-bit (x86-64): Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Linux Mint 21, Fedora 36 or newer.
      <strong>mpv required</strong>: <code>sudo apt install mpv</code> (or your distribution's
      <code>mpv</code> package). Make the file executable (<code>chmod +x</code>) then run it; the
      session is kept in the desktop keyring (GNOME Keyring, KWallet). The app updates itself if
      the AppImage is kept in a folder of your own (for example <code>~/Applications</code>).
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<p class="sg-meta" id="none" hidden>No version is available right now.</p>

<section class="sg-notes not-content" id="notes-card" hidden>
  <h2 id="notes-title">What's new</h2>
  <ul id="notes"></ul>
</section>

<script is:inline src="/download.js"></script>
